{"id":"word:hebrew:H6942","type":"word","title":"קָדַשׁ","subtitle":"H6942 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to be (causatively, make , pronounce or observe as) clean (ceremonially or morally)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to קָדַשׁ (H6942) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 173 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"קָדַשׁ (qâdash) means to be (causatively, make , pronounce or observe as) clean (ceremonially or morally) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 15 12."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"קָדַשׁ","transliteration":"qâdash","pronunciation":"kaw-dash'","strong":"H6942","lemmaId":"hebrew:H6942","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["וְ/קִדַּשְׁתָּ֥","מְקַדִּשְׁ/כֶֽם","מְקַדְּשָֽׁ/ם","וַ/יִּֽתְקַדְּשׁ֔וּ","הִקְדַּ֣שְׁתִּי"],"morphs":[["HVpv2mp",9],["HC/Vpq2ms",9],["HC/Vpw3ms",8],["HVhp3ms",7],["HVtv2mp",6],["HVhp1cs",6],["HR/Vpc",6],["HVhi3ms",6],["HVqi3ms",5],["HR/Vpc/Sp3ms",5]]},"definitions":{"short":"to be (causatively, make , pronounce or observe as) clean (ceremonially or morally)","usage":"appoint, bid, consecrate, dedicate, defile, hallow, (be, keep) holy(-er, place), keep, prepare, proclaim, purify, sanctify(-ied one, self), × wholly.","full":"H6942. qadash קָּדַשׁ verb denominative be set apart, consecrated (Gerber 238ff. ); — Qal Perfect 3masculine singular ׳ק Exod 29:21 ; suffix קְדַשְׁתִּיךָ Isa 65:5 ; 3 masculine plural קָדֵ֑שׁוּ Num 17:2 ; Imperfect 3masculine singular יִקְדַּשׁ 1Sam 21:6 ; יִקְדָּ֑שׁ Exod 29:37 +, etc.; — 1 be set apart, consecrated , hallowed, of shew-bread 1Sam 21:6 (dubious Passage, but compare especially RS Semitic i. 436; 2nd ed. 455 [also Dr sm.293 ], who proposes יְקֻדַּשׁ ); Aaron and his sons by blood Exod 29:21 (P); other persons Isa 65:5 (Di; but Pi`el Gei RS Semitic i. 431; 2nd ed. 451 Che Du Buhl). 2 be hallowed , by contact with sacred things, and so tabooed from profane use, of forfeited to sanctuary Exod 29:37 ; 30:29 ; Lev 6:11 ; 6:20 Num 17:2 ; 17:3 (P), Hag 2:12 . 3 consecrated, tabooed (above) Deut 22:9 (law against mixtures). Niph`al Perfect . 3 masculine singular נִקְדַּשׁ Isa 5:16 ; Exod 29:43 , etc.; Imperfect 3masculine singular וַיִּקָּדֵשׁ Num 20:13 ; 1 singular אֶקָּדֵשׁ Lev 10:3 ; Infinitive construct . suffix הִקָּֽדְשִׁי Ezek 36:23 ; 38:16 ; &#8212; 1 shew oneself sacred, majestic: c. בְּ person, + לְעֵינֵי Ezek 20:41 ; 28:25 ; 36:23 ; 38:16 ; 39:27 ; with בְּ Isa 5:16 ; Ezek 28:22 , compare Num 20:13 (P). 2 be honoured or treated as sacred || נכבד Lev 10:3 (P); opposed to חלּלשׁם 22:32 (P). 3 be consecrated, dedicated , by י ׳כבוד Exod 29:43 (P). Pi`el Perfect 3masculine singular קִדַּשׁ Num 6:11 ; 1Kin 8:64 , etc.; Imperfect 3masculine singular יְקַדֵּשׁ Gen 2:3 +, etc.; Imperative masculine singular קַדֵּשׁ Josh 7:13 ; קַדֶּשֿׁ Exod 13:2 , etc.; Infinitive construct קַדֵּשׁ 29:1 +, etc.; Participle מְקַדֵּשׁ 37:28 ; suffix מְקַדִּשְׁכֶם 31:13 +, etc.; — 1 set apart as sacred, consecrate, dedicate: a. places: Sinai Exod 19:23 (J), alter, etc., 29:36-37 , 30:29 (P), tabernacle, etc. 40:9-10 , 11 ; Lev 8:10-11 , 15 ; Num 7:1 (twice in verse) (P); tent of meeting Exod 29:44 (P); place of sacrifice 1Kin 8:64 2Chr 7:7 ; gate Neh 3:1 (twice in verse); &#8212; Ezek 7:24 see מִקְדָּשׁ below b. wave-offering Exod 29:27 (P). c. persons: priests Exod 28:3 , 41 ; 29:1 , 33 , 44 ; 30:30 ; 40:13 ; Lev 8:12 , 30 ; firstborn Exod 13:2 (P); keepers of ark 1Sam 7:1 . d. 7th day (by God) Gen 2:3 ; Exod 20:11 (P). 2 observe as holy, keep sacred: feasts, Sabbath Exod 20:8 = Deut 5:12 (Decal.), Jer 17:22 , 24 , 27 ; Ezek 20:20 ; 44:24 ; Neh 13:22 ; fast Joel 1:14 ; 2:15 ; year of Jubilee Lev 25:10 (P); so לבעל עצרה 2Kin 10:20 . 3 honour as sacred, hallow: a. God Deut 32:51 , his name Exod 36:23 . b priest Lev 21:8 (H). 4 consecrate by purification: a. places, house of ׳י 2Chr 29:5 , 17 (twice in verse), alter מִטֻּמְאֹת , Lev 16:19 . b. people העם Josh 7:13 (J), Ezek 44:10 ; 46:20 ; by washing Exod 19:10 , 14 (E); קהל for fast Joel 2:16 ; Nazirite Num 6:11 (P), sons of Job Job 1:5 ; family for sacrifice 1Sam 16:5 . c. war, or warriors, from custom of opening campaign by sacrifice , ( עַל ) ׳ק מִלְחָמָה Jer 6:4 ; Joel 4:9; Micah 3:5 ; Jer 22:7 ; 51:27-28 ,. d. of God, keeping his people pure and sacred: מְקַדֵּשׁ יהוה אני Exod 31:13 ; Lev 20:8 ; 21:8 , 15 , 23 ; 22:9 , 16 , 32 (H), Ezek 20:12 ; 37:28 . Pu`al Participle מְקֻדָּשׁ Ezek 48:11 , etc.; &#8212; consecrated, dedicated: priests 2Chr 26:18 ; Ezek 48:11 (read plural), things 2Chr 31:6 , feasts Ezra 3:5 , warriors Isa 13:3 . Hiph`il Perfect 3masculine singular הִקְדִּישׁ Zeph 1:7 +, etc.; Imperfect יַקְדּישׁ Lev 27:16 4 t., יַקְדִּשׁ 27:14 , etc.; Imperative suffix הַקְדִּשֵׁם Jer 12:3 ; Infinitive absolute הַקְדֵּשׁ Judg 17:3 ; construct הַקְדִּישׁ 2Chr 2:3 +, etc.; Participle מַקְדִּישׁ Lev 27:15 +, etc. 1 set apart, devote, consecrate: a. places, temple 2Chr 2:3 , city Josh 20:7 (P). b. things Exod 28:28 ; Lev 22:2-3 ,(P) 2Kin 12:19 ; 1Chr 23:13 ; 26:26-27 , 28 (twice in verse); Neh 12:47 (twice in verse); money Judg 17:3 (twice in verse); spoil 2Sam 8:11 (twice in verse) = 1Chr 18:11 ; field Lev 27:16-17 , 18 , 19 , 22 (H); house 27:14-15 , (H); firstlings Deut 15:19 (D) Lev 27:26 (H). c. of God: consecrate temple 1Kin 9:3 , 7 2Chr 7:16 , 20 ; 30:8 ; 36:14 ; prophet Jer 1:5 ; firstborn Num 3:13 ; 8:17 (P); devote wicked (as sheep) for sacrifice Jer 12:3 . 2 regard , or treat, as sacred, hallow: God Isa 8:13 ; 29:23 (twice in verse); + לְעֵינֵי person Num 20:12 ; 27:14 . 3 consecrate by purification: vessels 2Chr 29:19 ; persons for Passover 30:17 ; guests for sacrificial feast Zeph 1:7 (God subject). Hithpa`el Perfect , 1 singular הִתְקַדִּשְׁתִּי Ezek 38:23 , 2 masculine plural (consecutive) דִּשְׁתֶּם - Lev 11:44 ; 20:7 , 3 plural הִתְקַדָּ֑שׁוּ 2Chr 5:11 ; 30:17 , etc.; Imperfect 3masculine singular יִתְקַדְּשׁוּ 29:34 +; יִתְקַדָּ֑שׁוּ Exod 19:22 ; Imperative masculine plural הִתְקַדְּשׁוּ Num 11:18 +; הִתְקַדָּ֑שׁוּ Josh 3:5 ; Infinitive construct הִתְקַדֵּשֹׁ 2Chr 29:34 ; הִתְקַדֶּשֿׁ Isa 30:29 ; Perfect feminine singular מִתְקַדֶּשֶׁת 2Sam 11:4 ; plural מִתְקַדְּשִׁים Isa 66:17 ; &#8212; 1 keep oneself apart from unclean things Lev 11:44 ; 20:7 (P). 2 of God , cause himself to be hallowed , גּוֺיִם לְעֵינֵי Ezek 38:23 . 3 be observed as holy , of feast Isa 30:29 . 4 consecrate oneself by purification, of priests and Levites Exod 19:22 (J), 1Chr 15:12 , 14 ; 2Chr 5:11 ; 29:5 , 15 , 34 (twice in verse); 30:3 , 15 , 24 ; 31:18 ; 35:6 ; of people Num 11:18 ; Josh 3:5 ; 7:13 (J) 1Sam 16:5 ; 2Chr 30:17 ; Isa 66:17 ; woman 2Sam 11:4 she having ( just ) purified herself מִטֻּמְאָתָהּ Rs K. 276 Dr HPS.","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 15 12","keyReferences":["1Chr 15 12","1Chr 15 14","1Chr 18 11","1Chr 23 13","1Chr 26 26","1Chr 26 27","1Chr 26 28","1Chr 26 28"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":173,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 15 12","book":"1Chr","chapter":15,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הִֽתְקַדְּשׁוּ֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVtv2mp"},{"reference":"1Chr 15 14","book":"1Chr","chapter":15,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יִּֽתְקַדְּשׁ֔וּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vtw3mp"},{"reference":"1Chr 18 11","book":"1Chr","chapter":18,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הִקְדִּ֞ישׁ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVhp3ms"},{"reference":"1Chr 23 13","book":"1Chr","chapter":23,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְֽ/הַקְדִּישׁ/וֹ֩","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Vhc/Sp3ms"},{"reference":"1Chr 26 26","book":"1Chr","chapter":26,"verse":26,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הִקְדִּ֜ישׁ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVhp3ms"},{"reference":"1Chr 26 27","book":"1Chr","chapter":26,"verse":27,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הִקְדִּ֑ישׁוּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVhp3cp"},{